# Opposing Force M40A1 sniper rifle. Measured by vrcardgen, cut and carded by
# hand.
#
# THE ONE TRUE TWO-AXIS BOLT (M-03). Part K calls this the test that the joint
# model is general rather than a set of Half-Life special cases, and it is:
# lift the handle, pull back, push forward, drop. Every shot needs the full
# cycle.
#
# The model does not hand it over. `m40a1_bolt` is a single bone that both
# turns 0.595 radians and slides 1.25 units, in the same animation - and a
# part, to the renderer, is a lerp between two bracketed poses driven by one
# value. One bone cannot be two independent joints. (The two never-animated
# knobs are not the handle: they are the scope's windage and elevation
# turrets.)
#
# So the bolt is split, at load, by two operations:
#
#   the CARVE takes all 22 of the bolt's vertices onto a body of their own
#   that slides and does not turn;
#
#   the REWRITE replaces what is left - the handle - with a pure turn, so
#   that lifting it turns the bolt without also dragging it backwards.
#
# The body is parented to the handle, so lifting the handle turns the whole
# bolt, which is what a rifle does.
#
# JOINT ORDER IS NOT ARBITRARY. The `magazine_slide` preset makes joint 0 the
# action and joint 1 the magazine, so the bolt body has to be 0 and the clip
# 1 - the handle, which the preset knows nothing about, goes last. Numbering
# them the other way round silently gives the magazine the slide's catches.
#
# The plan's numbers check out: bolt 1.25 in `fire` and `reload2`, magazine
# 4.81. Both measured here to the hundredth.

weapon v_m40a1
match  bones 55  seqs 9  hash 0xb95673d5

# The bone every position in this card is measured in - the controls, the
# grab points, the chamber, the ejection port. Nothing recorded it until
# the engine had to place a control in the world to ask whether a thumb is
# near it; the simulator never needed one, because it never works in world
# space. Taken from the generator, which has always called this bone the
# WEAPON BODY and is what measured these numbers in the first place.
body   "m40a1_stock"

type   magazine_slide  capacity 5  rpm 40

# A BOLT ACTION CYCLES ITSELF FOR NOBODY, and it has no slide stop to hold
# open. Both of those are the preset's assumptions about a self-loader.
feed   no_self_loading  no_slide_lock

# The bolt's sliding body, cut out of the bolt.
synth m40a1_boltbody  from "m40a1_bolt"
      box   -1.20 0.20 -0.65   2.10 2.85 0.75
      pivot  0.00 0.00 0.00
      slide  axis 1.0 0.0 0.0   travel 1.25

# ...and the handle left behind, rewritten to turn and nothing else.
synth m40a1_bolt  from "m40a1_bolt"  rewrite
      hinge  axis 1.0 0.0 0.0   travel 0.60

# JOINT 0: the bolt, AND IT CANNOT MOVE UNTIL THE HANDLE IS UP. That is the
# gate from Part C, and this is the weapon it was written for.
joint 0  bone "m40a1_boltbody"  slide  travel 1.25  rest 0
    gate  2  0.80  1.00
    point eject at 0.80
    point feed  at 0.35
    grab  point 0.43 1.53 0.05  radius 2.0

# JOINT 1: five rounds, and the magazine comes out by hand like any other.
joint 1  bone "m40a1_clip"  slide  travel 4.81  rest 0
    grab  point 0.00 0.00 0.00  radius 2.0

# JOINT 2: the handle. Lift it and it stays lifted - there is no spring
# pulling a bolt handle down, which is why it carries no catch: its own
# stiffness against the hand is what holds it.
joint 2  bone "m40a1_bolt"  hinge  travel 0.60  rest 0
    # Stated, not assumed: silence means "use the default for this kind
    # of joint", and that default is a pistol slide's return - which is
    # exactly what the paragraph above says a bolt handle does not have.
    spring 0
    grab  point 0.43 1.53 0.05  radius 2.0
